{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(BS)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (BS)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Vieta&#39;s)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Vieta's)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Newton&#39;s_Sums)_(If_you_suck_at_factoring_like_me)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Newton's Sums) (If you suck at factoring like me)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Vieta_+_Factorization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Vieta + Factorization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(no_Vieta_+_not_quite_factoring)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (no Vieta + not quite factoring)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_StressedPineapple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_hurdler_(Jacob_Guo)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by hurdler (Jacob Guo)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f623238794914946de062cb4587aee863da93e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + kx + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. What is the sum<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/5018d7f4af85c4f6faba8cf5e5fca6ec10765cdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^3b^2 + a^2b^3 + b^3c^2 + b^2c^3 + c^3a^2 + c^2a^3?\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf08bfe2a2f664f08316f8b4ad622a7572d4868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~-k\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~-k+1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~1\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~k-1\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"462\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by factoring:\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n&amp;a^3b^2+a^2b^3+b^3c^2+b^2c^3+c^3a^2+c^2a^3 \\\\\n&amp;=a^2b^2(a+b)+b^2c^2(b+c)+c^2a^2(c+a)\\\\\n&amp;=(a^2b^2+b^2c^2+c^2a^2)(a+b+c) - a^2b^2c-b^2c^2a-c^2a^2b\\\\\n&amp;=(a^2b^2+b^2c^2+c^2a^2)(a+b+c) - (abc)(ab+bc+ca).\\\\\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\nFrom Vieta's Formulas, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d501f3412e3af870e232678a6b686d3cf311fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9fda3204f9165668ba94b4ca1cf112054fd628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ca = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8674b9d4b89fae9b3f3c5f7adfdc85abedf937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, the answer equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b285d59405ed695ae69e484fc8cf68f7eaf9fe14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2b^2+b^2c^2+c^2a^2)(0) - (-1)(k) = \\boxed{k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"313\" height=\"26\" /> \n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9b5cb6b20c28c0b4fd10fbf679ae16d2cd0033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\text{cyc}} a^2b^2(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"117\" height=\"45\" />.\nBy Vieta's (just like in solution 1), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4b4a0b6f34071ebc2f7eeb0ffa12702ca0aae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3faf77056b16cf568b71b2a039b80550c84bf3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf596eff7fee9b9b138f06c0d6144fb1aa7b9637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ac=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, so this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552b18353f7b64fe259d5a0e39e826cf4c1dadc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\text{cyc}} -a^2b^2c = \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} -(abc)(ab) = \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} ab = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"328\" height=\"45\" /> by Vieta's.\n~ScoutViolet\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28BS.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(BS)\">Solution 3 (BS)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (BS)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let’s just pick a nice and convenient a, b, c. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56da092ee9f585206703494c0e8df2c567a1dda1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot2^{-\\frac13}-2^\\frac23=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"21\" />, so we can just have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0375c800d3a663fddef3344f49c82eab3902a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)=(2^{-\\frac13}, 2^{-\\frac13},-2^\\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"24\" />). So expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c4905426f0eeedc33ae16591c11df78ce18b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-a)(x-b)(x-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4bbefc6f3fddfdde2d906e76e79d1c45dc1033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-3\\cdot2^{-\\frac23}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"21\" />. Evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9bcf6eedffde5b067ee9c414a8492f90586ba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^2 + a^2b^3 + b^3c^2 + b^2c^3 + c^3a^2 + c^2a^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/69953d8f6a68ea1caf8594e50ce71551af1bedfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^5+2a^2c^3+2a^3c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403983cde6b4712662e439d3b528eb49abb5a5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3\\cdot2^{-\\frac23}=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b346611c839b9f6a1ace80b3f3e684aec9ea373e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textit{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" />. (i did this on the actual test)\n</p><p>~benjamintontungtungtungsahur\n</p><p>who is going to think of this on the test bro 😭😭 \nand change ur username dawg 🥀🥀\n</p><p>this solution is acc so fire leave him alone\n</p><p>yo lowk it's acc so fire that the entire tung tung tung sahor family agreed (they told me) and EVERYONE is going to think of this on the test (because, y'know, I totally didn't factor then use Vieta in a few secs *cough *cough) and his username is tuff idk what the first guy was on abt\n</p><p>tbh this sol was my first thought\n</p><p>I agree with the first guy bro rly needs to change his username  💀\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Vieta.27s.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Vieta's)\">Solution 4 (Vieta's)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Vieta&#39;s)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec3875a9e546fdafa479d865b218c7d771a50f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc} ab = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"82\" height=\"45\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3faf77056b16cf568b71b2a039b80550c84bf3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. We can factor the original expression into:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f314d1dd52552e84584aa1cc13d41d8e1cd9c957.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} a^2b^2(a+b) = \\sum_{cyc} \\left(-\\frac{1}{c}\\right)^2(-c) = -\\frac{\\sum_{cyc} ab}{abc} = \\boxed{\\text{(E) } k.}\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>~ABC09090927\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Newton.27s_Sums.29_.28If_you_suck_at_factoring_like_me.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Newton's_Sums)_(If_you_suck_at_factoring_like_me)\">Solution 5 (Newton's Sums) (If you suck at factoring like me)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Newton&#39;s Sums) (If you suck at factoring like me)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db2a350751ead9350677a7eef0a5de9e713e097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^2+a^2b^3+b^3c^2+b^2c^3+c^3a^2+c^2a^3 = (a^3+b^3+c^3)(a^2+b^2+c^2)-(a^5+b^5+c^5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"669\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>By Newton's sums, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3553edf4ad11d40f20927e0fea8a8026102739f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + k(a+b+c) + 3 = 0\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c71fbbff59feb25e20e613a6cb9316af7edf4a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^5 + b^5 + c^5) + k(a^3+b^3+c^3) + 1(a^2+b^2+c^2) = 0\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491c5d5a5e7e668d504848546090f0c3a6725e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab+bc+ca)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"350\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>From Vieta's formulas, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d501f3412e3af870e232678a6b686d3cf311fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea5869514edbb4e92b72c233a7bb87383bd4e5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Solving, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6280ae026ac112d53a64994c590d4026c2d3a3b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) = -3\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37d021e4900dea4e745cddfebc6c9b22796d84da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^2 + b^2 + c^2) = -2k\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/3605fcc1e43b727a21161166c24a8cb8aebef105.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^5 + b^5 + c^5) - 3k - 2k = 0 \\to (a^5 + b^5 + c^5) = 5k\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd802490932c03898123bacfa53ce56ce9b0534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^2+a^2b^3+b^3c^2+b^2c^3+c^3a^2+c^2a^3 = (-3)(-2k)-5k = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"533\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ku220\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we begin by factoring:\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n&amp;a^3b^2+a^2b^3+b^3c^2+b^2c^3+c^3a^2+c^2a^3 \\\\\n&amp;=a^2b^2(a+b)+b^2c^2(b+c)+c^2a^2(c+a)\\\\\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\nFrom Vieta's Formulas, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d501f3412e3af870e232678a6b686d3cf311fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9fda3204f9165668ba94b4ca1cf112054fd628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ca = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8674b9d4b89fae9b3f3c5f7adfdc85abedf937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d501f3412e3af870e232678a6b686d3cf311fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c404a8a52feff23fff1ac703d849a32e065d0d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, then isolating one variable each time yields:\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n&amp;=-\\frac{1}{c^2}(a+b)-\\frac{1}{a^2}(b+c)-\\frac{1}{b^2}(c+a)\\\\\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Isolating a + b + c = 0, you get\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n&amp;=-\\frac{1}{c^2}(-c)-\\frac{1}{a^2}(-a)-\\frac{1}{b^2}(-b)\\\\\n&amp;=-(\\frac{ab+bc+ac}{abc})\\\\\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>This simplifies to:\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n&amp;=-(\\frac{k}{-1})\\\\\n&amp;=k\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer equals = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883acbde5519f0db9785e9b63d772ce05cdfa1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~BOTNATE\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Vieta_.2B_Factorization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Vieta_+_Factorization)\">Solution 7 (Vieta + Factorization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Vieta + Factorization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can easily factor the expression into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57ffaf40f99b4a15c8341b5005e1a773497fcc65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2b^2(a+b)+b^2c^2(b+c)+a^2c^2(a+c)\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By Vieta, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, so we can rewrite the expression into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db609f9df8f5a45df7b17330dc61be1bdbbc0df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2(-c)+b^2c^2(-a)+a^2c^2(-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" /> which is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbbffceea2f5804ef9c4dfbb924cf2a5771d078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-abc(ab+bc+ac)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />. By Vieta we also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3faf77056b16cf568b71b2a039b80550c84bf3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf596eff7fee9b9b138f06c0d6144fb1aa7b9637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ac=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore the expression is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128926614dc83ae4dd639bff9ba75720c9b7113e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(-1)k=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883acbde5519f0db9785e9b63d772ce05cdfa1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{k}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~backtosq-1\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28no_Vieta_.2B_not_quite_factoring.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(no_Vieta_+_not_quite_factoring)\">Solution 8 (no Vieta + not quite factoring)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (no Vieta + not quite factoring)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the expression we are asked to evaluate equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bba6b24cd4e0dc9862a5e1edd4e431b0780cec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+kx+1=(x-a)(x-b)(x-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"283\" height=\"21\" />. Expanding the right hand side yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a96f71564ac7200ec4716086b0bef0576aade78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-x^2(a+b+c)+x(ac+bc+ab)-abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"21\" />. Equating coefficients, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294caccf17e57887f1bfa495a819593c3b060cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac+bc+ab=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3faf77056b16cf568b71b2a039b80550c84bf3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>We may find the first equation helpful for cancelling things out, so let us fiddle around with it, trying to piece out as much of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as possible: we discover that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975adce3627fdf796f80a5e3e18bd7ccab8fc52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c)(ab)^2=a^3b^2+a^2b^3+c(ab)^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"338\" height=\"21\" />, which shares terms with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c18f1feb8c99535184ab02829a1fb8d501edf59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c)(bc)^2=b^3c^2+b^2c^3+a(bc)^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/76483442756845cf0f8b3ede173d66c8b8035b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c)(ac)^2=a^3c^2+a^2c^3+b(ac)^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"338\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Adding the three equations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77391baa7b1f0300d5ba4f6e06cfefb40347498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+a(bc)^2+b(ac)^2+c(ab)^2=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"257\" height=\"21\" /> Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9cf9c5281be7a31cb5dbab3bde9033c3f27251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(bc)^2+b(ac)^2+c(ab)^2=(abc)(ac+bc+ab)=-1(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"431\" height=\"21\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f86d454d5ac5c67a4016f4b1ae0aa49cfb05070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8a3230e902beb040885c91b6c68d332f4a1afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\boxed{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"26\" />. \n</p><p>~iluminate\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn.org\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FuJbXC8x-R\">https://youtu.be/FuJbXC8x-R</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_StressedPineapple\">Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=NWBPm3lThH4&amp;t=319s\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=NWBPm3lThH4&amp;t=319s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xipj4q--LCk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xipj4q--LCk</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_Continuum_Math\">Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 by Continuum Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BwwvBtqSql4?si=8ei6YchQZjxQOwvh\">https://youtu.be/BwwvBtqSql4?si=8ei6YchQZjxQOwvh</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4zL9jFvxjJg\">https://youtu.be/4zL9jFvxjJg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_hurdler_.28Jacob_Guo.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_hurdler_(Jacob_Guo)\">Video Solution by hurdler (Jacob Guo)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by hurdler (Jacob Guo)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gMVO6T-tJOc\">https://youtu.be/gMVO6T-tJOc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-